  "humanReadable": {
    "plainEnglishSummary": "This manifest defines how Xtrata-native .x names work. A registry contract proves who owns each name. A resolver manifest explains what that name points to. Other Xtrata manifests can link themselves to names through the xns extension.",
    "developerSummary": "Normalize the name, hash it, read the registry record, fetch the resolver manifest, verify hashes, then resolve linked manifests or records.",
    "marketplaceSummary": "Display .x names only after registry verification. Names may be saleable if the registry supports transfer. Linked collections should be loaded through the resolver manifest.",
    "walletSummary": "Use .x names for display and sending only after forward and reverse resolution checks pass.",
    "archivistSummary": "The namespace manifest records the naming rules and resolver standard; historical changes should be captured through registry events and inscribed amendments."
